  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: fcd19b51b53d4f5a91a947cf67c81c88, type: 3}
  m_Name: FovereInventory
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Fovere.DialogueData
  conversationBlock:
  - Hi. <pause=0.5>You may not know it, <pause=0.5>however you have an Inventory!
    <pause=0.5>You aren't able to access it at this time, <pause=0.5>but there is
    a system behind it.
  - Every item you pick up in this game gets stored in your inventory. <pause=0.5>It's
    a fixed set of slots, <pause=0.5>starting with 16. <pause=0.5>However, <pause=0.5>there
    is implementation to allow you to expand your inventory as you progress the game!
  - Each slot holds one type of item, <pause=0.5>and items can stack up to a maximum
    amount. <pause=0.5>If a stack is already in your inventory, <pause=0.5>new items
    will fill that stack before taking up a new slot.
  - Removing items works in reverse! <pause=0.5>The system finds every stack of that
    item and draws from them in order, <pause=0.5>until the requested amount has
    been taken [or finds there aren't enough].
  - Nothing gets silently deleted either! <pause=0.5>If the system tries to remove
    more than you have, <pause=0.5>the whole operation is denied. <pause=0.5>You'll
    never find an incorrect state in there!
  - The inventory is also saved and restored between our sessions! <pause=0.5>If
    you want more information on how we handle persistant data, <pause=0.5>find the
    database resident! <pause=0.5>They'll tell you all about it.
  - Thanks for talking to me! <pause=0.5>I love explaining this system. <pause=0.5>Maybe
    go talking to other residents to find out more about the game.
